    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A savory breakfast skillet built for a slow weekend morning: golden, crisp Yukon Gold potatoes, big flakes of our smoked rainbow trout, soft-baked eggs with jammy yolks, fresh herbs and creamy goat cheese. Miriam finishes it with small spoonfuls of salmon roe for a little burst of salinity.</p><p>It all happens in one cast-iron skillet. Parboil the potatoes, crisp them in butter, fold in the trout, crack the eggs into wells and let the oven do the rest. Serve it straight from the pan.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
